            <ArticleTitle>Air filters and air cleaners: rostrum by the American Academy of Allergy, Asthma &amp; Immunology Indoor Allergen Committee.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaci.2009.08.036</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The allergist is generally recognized as possessing the greatest expertise in relating airborne contaminants to respiratory health, both atopic and nonatopic. Consequently, allergists are most often asked for their professional opinions regarding the appropriate use of air-cleaning equipment. This rostrum serves as a resource for the allergist and other health care professionals seeking a better understanding of air filtration.</AbstractText>
